.TH "server_shutdown" "3" "2026\-02\-01" "bash\-server 0.1.0" "bash\-server library"
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
#include \(dqserver.h\(dq

void server_shutdown(void);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Performs a clean shutdown of the bash\-server, releasing all
server\-level resources.
This function is called from the main accept loop when
\f[CR]server_running\f[R] becomes \f[CR]0\f[R] (set by
\f[CR]server_signal_handler()\f[R] on \f[CR]SIGINT\f[R] or
\f[CR]SIGTERM\f[R]).
.PP
The shutdown sequence is:
.IP "1." 3
\f[B]Close listening socket\f[R]: Calls
\f[CR]server_socket_close(server_fd, config.socket_path)\f[R] to close
the socket file descriptor and remove the socket file from the
filesystem.
Sets \f[CR]server_fd = \-1\f[R].
.IP "2." 3
\f[B]Remove token file\f[R]: If \f[CR]config.auth_file\f[R] is set,
calls \f[CR]unlink(config.auth_file)\f[R] to remove the authentication
token file (\f[CR]<socket_path>.token\f[R]).
.IP "3." 3
\f[B]Remove PID file\f[R]: If \f[CR]config.pid_file\f[R] is set, calls
\f[CR]unlink(config.pid_file)\f[R] to remove the PID file.
.IP "4." 3
\f[B]Reap children\f[R]: Calls \f[CR]reap_children()\f[R] to collect
exit status of any remaining session child processes via
\f[CR]waitpid()\f[R] with \f[CR]WNOHANG\f[R].
.SH PARAMETERS
None.
Operates on the file\-scoped global variables \f[CR]server_fd\f[R] and
\f[CR]config\f[R] in \f[CR]server_main.c\f[R].
.SH RETURN VALUE
None.
.SH ERRORS
Errors during cleanup (e.g., \f[CR]unlink()\f[R] failing because a file
was already removed) are silently ignored.
Shutdown is best\-effort.
.SH SEE ALSO
\f[CR]server_socket_close\f[R](3), \f[CR]server_signal_handler\f[R](3),
\f[CR]server_daemonize\f[R](3), \f[CR]server_socket_create\f[R](3)
.SH NOTES
This function handles cleanup for the \f[B]socket transport\f[R] mode
only.
The named pipe transport mode (\f[CR]\-\-named\-pipe\f[R]) has its own
inline cleanup in \f[CR]run_named_pipe_server()\f[R].
The stdio/fd transport modes do not create socket or token files, so
\f[CR]server_shutdown()\f[R] is not called for them.
.PP
Child process reaping uses \f[CR]waitpid(\-1, &status, WNOHANG)\f[R] in
a loop, which collects all terminated children without blocking.
Any children still running at shutdown time will be orphaned
(re\-parented to init/PID 1) and continue until they exit naturally or
are killed externally.
.PP
The function does not remove the parent directory of the socket file.
On systems using \f[CR]$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR\f[R], the directory is managed
by the session infrastructure.
On fallback to \f[CR]/tmp/bash\-server\-<uid>/\f[R], the directory
persists until system cleanup.
.PP
The \f[CR]config\f[R] structure\(cqs heap\-allocated fields
(\f[CR]auth_token\f[R], \f[CR]auth_file\f[R], \f[CR]socket_path\f[R])
are not freed, since \f[CR]server_shutdown()\f[R] is followed
immediately by process exit.
